## Key Concepts

- A custom AI model can be connected to a website or program.
- The tic-tac-toe model was told to return one move as a row and column.
- The game board had to be changed into text before sending it to the AI.
- Ollama can be called through an API from a local program.
- The program has to read the AI response and turn it back into a game move.
- Small AI models do not always follow instructions correctly.
- AI does not remember past messages unless the history is sent again.
- AI is not always better than normal programming.

## How the Tic-Tac-Toe AI Works

The class used a custom Ollama model to play tic-tac-toe.

The website keeps track of the game board. When it is the AI's turn, the board is changed into text and sent to the model. The AI is supposed to answer with a move such as `2,2`.

The program then reads that answer and places the AI move on the board.

