## Problems With the AI

* The AI sometimes returned extra words instead of only numbers.
* It sometimes picked a space that was already taken.
* A bad response could cause the game to stop working.
* The small model could only play a few moves correctly sometimes.
* A larger model or better system prompt could improve the results.
* The program could also retry when the AI gives a bad answer.

## Why Normal Code Can Be Better

The normal tic-tac-toe version used a small amount of JavaScript and ran very quickly.

The AI version needed a large model running in memory and was less reliable. This showed that adding AI does not automatically make a program better. Sometimes simple code is the better choice.

